# VisualSeek: AI-Powered Visual Similarity & Semantic Search Engine

[![Python 3.10+](https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.10+-blue.svg)](https://www.python.org/downloads/)
[![PyTorch](https://img.shields.io/badge/PyTorch-2.0+-ee4c2c.svg)](https://pytorch.org/)
[![FAISS](https://img.shields.io/badge/FAISS-Vector%20Search-green.svg)](https://github.com/facebookresearch/faiss)
[![Streamlit](https://img.shields.io/badge/Streamlit-UI-FF4B4B.svg)](https://streamlit.io/)
[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](LICENSE)

VisualSeek is an end-to-end computer vision and semantic retrieval platform built around deep vision-language representations (CLIP), vector similarity indexing (FAISS & exact cosine search), dimensionality reduction (PCA, t-SNE, UMAP), and real-time interactive exploration.

---

## Architecture Overview

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    subgraph Data Pipeline
        A[Stanford Dogs Dataset\n20,580 images · 120 breeds] --> B[Dynamic Dataset Discovery]
        B --> C[Stratified Sampling & Validation]
        C --> D[Torch Preprocessing Pipeline]
    end

    subgraph Feature Representation
        D --> E[OpenAI CLIP ViT-B/32 Encoder]
        D --> F[Color & Texture Histogram Baseline]
        E --> G[L2 Normalized Embeddings\n512 Dimensions]
        G --> H[Artifact Storage Cache\n.npz & .parquet]
    end

    subgraph Search & Retrieval
        H --> I[FAISS IndexFlatIP\nCosine Similarity]
        H --> J[Brute-Force NumPy Search]
        K[Image Query] --> E
        L[Text Query] --> M[CLIP Text Encoder]
        E --> N[Query Vector]
        M --> N
        N --> I
        N --> J
        I --> O[Top-K Ranked Results]
        J --> O
    end

    subgraph Latent Space Exploration
        H --> P[PCA 2D/3D & Variance Ratios]
        H --> Q[t-SNE Non-Linear Manifold]
        H --> R[UMAP Topological Embedding]
    end

    subgraph Interactive UI
        O --> S[Streamlit Application]
        P --> T[Plotly Embedding Explorer]
        Q --> T
        R --> T
        S --> U[Visual Search]
        S --> V[Semantic Text Search]
        S --> T
        S --> W[System & Retrieval Analytics]
    end
```

---

## Core Features

- **🔎 Visual Similarity Search**: Upload any dog image to retrieve Top-K visually and semantically similar images with similarity percentage scores and breed classifications.
- **💬 Semantic Natural Language Search**: Query images using plain text descriptions (e.g., *"white fluffy dog running on grass"*, *"spotted dalmatian"*) using joint vision-language text-to-image projections.
- **🧭 Interactive Embedding Explorer**: Inspect 512-dimensional vector spaces projected into 2D and 3D via PCA, t-SNE, and UMAP using responsive Plotly scatter plots with breed clustering and thumbnail metadata.
- **📈 PCA Explained Variance**: Real calculated scree plots and cumulative explained variance curves.
- **📊 Real Analytics & Benchmarks**: Latency tracking, Precision@1, Precision@5, Precision@10, and empirical comparisons between Baseline histograms and CLIP representations. No fabricated metrics.
- **⚙️ Dual Search Modes**: Switch dynamically between FAISS indexing and exact Brute-Force Cosine retrieval.
- **⚡ Dual Runtime Modes**: Built-in development mode (`limit: 1000`) for rapid local iteration, seamlessly switchable to the full 20,580-image dataset (`limit: null`).

---

## Tech Stack

| Component | Technology |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Language** | Python 3.10+ (tested on Python 3.13) |
| **Vision-Language Model** | OpenAI CLIP ViT-B/32 via `open_clip_torch` |
| **Vector Search** | Facebook AI Similarity Search (`faiss-cpu`) |
| **Dimensionality Reduction** | Scikit-Learn (`PCA`, `TSNE`) |
| **Deep Learning Framework** | PyTorch (`torch`, `torchvision`) |
| **Interactive UI** | Streamlit, Plotly Express & Graph Objects |
| **Data Processing & Testing** | NumPy, SciPy, Pillow, Pydantic, PyYAML, Pytest |

---

## Dataset

VisualSeek automatically detects and indexes the **Stanford Dogs Dataset**:
- **Total Images**: 20,580 JPEG images
- **Classes**: 120 recognized dog breeds
- **Annotations**: PASCAL VOC XML bounding box annotations

The system includes a zero-config dynamic discovery engine that crawls parent directories and detects dataset layouts without hardcoding fragile Kaggle paths.

